# The written start-up state (and the state every fork child reads): what `cargo xtask so` moves into the `.data1` cluster (xtask/src/coldbss.rs
# `move_startup_state`; D-X.64, LAYOUT-DATA-CLUSTERS-6). Declared by hand, never generated: placement follows
# this list, not a trace of the current layout, so it is the same in every profile and every build. The check
# is a test: hot_text_products `init_startup_data_accesses_are_in_the_data1_cluster` traces `page_faults true`
# (every writable input section on a 64 KiB boundary of its own) and names any small static start-up touches
# outside `.data1`; declare it here. `init_written_startup_objects_are_in_the_data1_cluster` checks every entry
# is defined and in `.data1`.
# Entries, one per line (text after `#` is a comment):
#   <crate>::<path>::<STATIC>  a Rust static, and every part LLVM splits it into (`.0`, `.1.llvm.<n>`)
#   symbol <name>              an object in a section of its own name, `.data.<name>` or `.bss.<name>` (ABI names)
#   section <name>             an object in a section of another name (C)
# An entry must name at least one section in every profile, unless it ends with `fast-only` (the release
# profile's LTO folds it away). A matched section over 8 KiB is refused (the cluster would spread over pages).

# CPU feature detection and the copy/fill thresholds it sets (every start).
liella_boundary::cpu::DETECTIONS
liella_boundary::cpu::FEATURES
liella_boundary::cpu::FEATURES_READY
liella_boundary::cpu::STATE
